-- `boundary.md` §9.2's runtime module: the platform `views` names `ssr` with
-- a runtime split between `markup.js` and the module `Views` (not `Rt`: since
-- 2026-11-03 `node` owns that module name). `Views`'s `list`
-- stands in for the lowering's three-argument export and takes two —
-- `foreign_arity_mismatch` at the declaration — and `markup.js` imports
-- `missing` from `beni:Views`, which `Views` does not declare —
-- `foreign_unbound_reference` at the name. `escape`, which `Views` supplies
-- and `markup.js` does not export, is no mismatch. Nothing is written.
import Node exposing (Program)


main : Program
main = Node.print "hello"
